== Purpose ==
Encode a private social opening as exact bytes and derive the two u128
arguments accepted by SocialReceiptRegistry.ko. This is a Konaet application
format; it is not a Bitcoin BIP and does not change the consensus protocol.

== Input ==
An ASCII stream of exactly three LF-terminated lines, with no CR, BOM,
whitespace suffixes or trailing records:
# A salt of exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters (32 bytes).
# Opaque canonical document bytes encoded as 4 to 32768 lowercase hex characters,
  with even length (2 to 16384 bytes).
# An expected digest of exactly 64 lowercase hex characters, or a single dash.

The complete stream is bounded at 32900 bytes. Hex decoding MUST reject
uppercase, non-hex symbols and odd length. Implementations MUST reject
malformed input before producing any result. The SDK, not these clients,
performs JSON normalization. Salt generation for real openings MUST use a
cryptographically secure random generator and MUST produce 32 bytes.

== Commitment ==
Let S be the decoded salt and D the decoded document. Let P be the ASCII
bytes of KONAET/SOCIAL-RECEIPT/v1 followed by one zero byte.

<pre>
C = SHA-256(P || S || D)
high = unsigned big-endian integer C[0..15]
low  = unsigned big-endian integer C[16..31]
</pre>

Both integers are printed as exact decimal strings in the interval
0 through 2^128-1. No floating-point conversion, truncation or signed
interpretation is permitted. Every bit of C is retained by the pair.

== Output and exit status ==
The output is one JSON object with commitment (64 lowercase hex characters),
args (two decimal strings) and matches (true, false or null). Output key
order is not significant. With a dash reference matches is null and exit
status is zero. A correct reference yields true and zero. A different
reference yields false and one. Invalid input yields exit two, no standard
output and a bounded error on standard error.

== Security boundary ==
The stream contains the private opening material; do not expose it in logs
or process arguments. Use stdin. A matching hash proves an opening matches
the supplied digest, not inclusion in a ledger, legal authorship or truth
of the document. Inclusion and finality require the separate consensus
verifier with trusted genesis and contract identifiers. The salt does not
hide the operator's public signing address. SHA-256 is used from existing
cryptographic libraries; this specification introduces no new hash function.

== Conformance ==
All executable clients share 12 SDK-generated synthetic vectors, mismatch
checks, 20 malformed-input cases and the 16 KiB boundary test. Their output
is submitted to the real .ko registry in a four-process permissioned network
and its quorum certificate is checked by the existing Node verifier.
C and C++ checks additionally use address and undefined-behavior sanitizers.

== Node membership ==
Public code does not grant a validator identity. An existing network's
genesis and its configured validator roster determine consensus membership.
The registry owner controls write authorization. The ISC software license
continues to apply to copying, use and modification of this distribution.
